commit fd2310c74ed7b7fdb34b16fb13556d0063859ab1
Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 09:40:08 2026 +0800

    feat(run): vector-capable fast default; clearer engine messages

    Three related improvements to `run`'s engine handling:

    - Default the standalone fast cpu to the vector-capable andes-ax46mpv (rv64)
      / andes-a46mpv (rv32), replacing the non-vector andes-ax45 / andes-a45. RVV
      binaries now run on fast out of the box at the cpu model's built-in VLEN;
      andesim still passes NO vlen of its own (a user pins an exact width via the
      post-`--` -cpu, which wins). Both names verified to boot the vplat fixtures.

    - resolve_accurate_engine served both cycle and hybrid but hardcoded "model
      cycle needs a cycle-accurate engine"; reword to "a cycle-accurate engine is
      required" so `--mode hybrid --engine qemu64` no longer says "cycle".

    - normalize_engine_label now maps the trigger name "csr" -> "marker" (like
      verilator -> vsim), so list/doctor speak the CLI's `--trigger marker`
      vocabulary instead of the engine's internal "csr".

    Tests: engine_registry_test covers the new defaults, the mode-agnostic error,
    and the csr->marker normalization. USER_GUIDE fast-default section updated.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

